83esponsoring body.2 aTurner-Fairbank Highway Research Center,0https://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/n82270079eissuing body.2 aERES Consultants, Inc.0https://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/n8410845208iPrint version:tDesign and construction of PCC pavementsw(OCoLC)4574448608iMicrofiche version:tDesign and construction of PCC pavementsw(OCoLC)4266532540uhttps://purl.fdlp.gov/GPO/gpo923274 zAddress at time of PURL creation3Volume Iuhttps://www.fhwa.dot.gov/publications/research/infrastructure/pavements/pccp/98052/98052.pdf4 zAddress at time of PURL creation3Volume IIuhttps://www.fhwa.dot.gov/publications/research/infrastructure/pavements/pccp/98127/98127.pdf4 zAddress at time of PURL creation3Volume IIIuhttps://www.fhwa.dot.gov/publications/research/infrastructure/pavements/ltpp/98113/98113.pdf  3(online)uhttps://catalog.gpo.gov/fdlpdir/locate.jsp?ItemNumber=0982-G-11&SYS=001057969  aC0bGPO  aXZL4  abc76 20180521b2018052103850cam a2200577Ii 00105797320191121112338.0m     o  d f      cr bn||||||abpcr bn||||||ada160525e199909  vaua    obt  f000 0 eng d  a(OCoLC)950574507  aOCLCEbengerdaepncOCLCEdOCLCQdGPO 4aTE251.5b.S88 1999  a0982-G-11 (online)0 aTD 2.30:99-0740 aTD 2.30:99-0751 aRada, Gonzalo R.,10aStudy of LTPP distress data variability /c[G.R. Rada and five others].3 aStudy of Long Term Pavement Performance distress data variability 1aMcLean, VA :bU.S. Department Transportation, Federal Highway Administration, Research, Development, and Technology, Turner-Fairbank Highway Research Center,cSeptember 1999.  a1 online resource (2 volumes) :billustrations  atextbtxt2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier  aFinal report;bJanuary 1997-December 1998.  aDescription based on online resource; title from PDF cover (FHWA.DOT.gov website, viewed May 21, 2018).  aSponsored by Office of Infrastructure Research and Development, Federal Highway AdministrationbDTFH61-97-C-00002.  a"September 1999."  a"Performing organization: Law PCS, a division of LAW Engineering and Environmental Services, Inc."--Report documentation page.  a"Contracting officer's rechnical representative - Monte Symons"--Report documentation page.  a"Publication no. FHWA-RD-99-074."  a"Publication no. FHWA-RD-99-075."  aReliable distress data for pavement performance model development and validation, and other pavement engineering products, are critical to the success of the Long-Term Pavement Performance (LTPP) program. Confidence in distress data requires a measure of error because of the bias and precision components of its variability. No systematic evaluation has been performed to quantify the bias and variability associated with both the manual and PASCO film-based distress data. In view of this, this study was undertaken by the Federal Highway Administration (FHWA) to assess the variability of the LTPP distress data, including those in the Information Management System (IMS) and those currently being collected using either photographic or manual methods.  aIncludes bibliographical references (volume 1, page 137).00gvolume I.t[Without special title] --gvolume II.tAppendix A, Appendix B, and Appendix C.20aLong-Term Pavement Performance Program (U.S.)0https://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/no98068869 0aPavementsxPerformancexMathematical models. 0aPavementsxEvaluationxMathematical models. 0aPavementsxMaintenance and repairxMathematical models.2 aTurner-Fairbank Highway Research Center,0https://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/n82270079eissuing body.2 aLaw PCS (Firm)08iPrint version:tStudy of LTPP distress data variabilityw(OCoLC)4269090008iMicrofiche version:tStudy of LTPP distress data variabilityw(OCoLC)4355228040uhttps://purl.fdlp.gov/GPO/gpo923014 zAddress at time of PURL creation3Volume Iuhttps://www.fhwa.dot.gov/publications/research/infrastructure/pavements/ltpp/99074/99074.pdf4 zAddress at tim