  ot   f000 0 eng d  a(OCoLC)1038275002  aGPObengerdaepncGPO  a0982-G-11 (online)0 aTD 2.30:98-0941 aJiang, Jane,10aMechanistic evaluation of test data from LTPP jointed concrete pavement test sections /cY. Jane Jiang, Shiraz D. Tayabji, and Chung L. Wu. 1aMcClean, VA :bU.S. Department of Transportation, Federal Highway Administration, Research and Development, Turner-Fairbank Highway Research Center,cJune 1998.  a1 online resource (78 unnumbered pages) :billustrations  atextbtxt2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier  aFinal Report;bFeb 1995-Dec 1997.  aDescription based on online resource; title from PDF cover (FHWA.DOT.gov website, viewed June 01, 2018).  aSponsored by Office of Research and Development, Federal Highway AdministrationbDTFH61-95-C-00028.  a"Performing organization: ERES Consultants, Inc."--Technical report documentation page.  a"This study has shown that, even given the many current limitations in the LTPP database, the LTPP data can be used successfully to develop better insight into pavement behavior and to improve pavement performance"--Technical report documentation page.  a"Publication no. FHWA-RD-98-094."  a"June 1998."20aLong-Term Pavement Performance Program (U.S.)0https://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/no98068869 0aPavementsxPerformance.0https://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh85098841 0aPavementsxTesting.0https://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh850988441 aTayabji, S. D.q(Shiraz D.),0https://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/n85005582eauthor.1 aWu, Chung L.,eauthor.2 aERES Consultants, Inc.0https://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/n841084522 aTurner-Fairbank Highway Research Center,0https://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/n82270079eissuing body.40uhttps://purl.fdlp.gov/GPO/gpo923994 zAddress at time of PURL creationuhttps://www.fhwa.dot.gov/publications/research/infrastructure/pavements/ltpp/98094/  3(online)uhttps://catalog.gpo.gov/fdlpdir/locate.jsp?ItemNumber=0982-G-11&SYS=001059485  aC0bGPO  aXZL4  abc76 20180601b20180601  aPERM_INGEST_0428202203895nam a2200541Ii 00105956220180601135538.0m     o  d f      cr |||||||||||180601e199909  vauab   obt  f000 0 eng d  a(OCoLC)1038278279  aGPObengerdaepncGPO  a0982-G-11 (online)0 aTD 2.30:99-0881 aAli, Hesham A.,10aDetermination of frost penetration in LTPP test sections, final report /cHesham A. Ali and Shiraz D. Tayabji.3 aDetermination of frost penetration in Long Term Pavement Performance sections 1aMcLean, VA :bU.S. Department of Transportation, Federal Highway Administration, Research, Development, and Technology, Turner-Fairbank Highway Research Center,cSeptember 1999.  a1 online resource (138 unnumbered pages) :billustrations, map  atextbtxt2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier  aFinal report;bAug. 1997- July 1998.  aDescription based on online resource; title from PDF cover (FHWA.DOT.gov website, viewed June 01, 2018).  a"Performing organization: ERES Consultants, Inc."--Technical report documentation page.  a"Contracting Officer's Technical Representative (COTR): Cheryl Allen Richter"--Technical report documentation page.  a"September 1999."  aIncludes tables.  a"Publication no. FHWA-RD-99-088."  aThe main goal of the study reported here was to determine frost penetration at the selected Seasonal Monitoring Program (SMP) sections. As part of the study, an interactive computer program, FROST, was developed to facilitate the interpretation of the electrical resistivity and temperature data. Analysis results include the freeze state at each electrical resistivity sensor and the frost penetration at each site. As part of the overall LTPP data analysis effort, it is expected that the information on the seasonal variation in the freeze state in the unbound base, subbase, and subgrade will be used to develop improved understanding of the seasonal variation in the load-carrying capacity of pavements and the subsequent effect on pavement performance.  aIncludes bibliographical references (pages 53-54.).  aSponsored by Office of Infrastructure Research and Development, Federal Highway AdministrationbDTFH61-96-C-0000320aLong-Term Pavement Performance Program (U.S.)0https://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/no98068869 0aPavementsxFrost damagexTesting. 0aPavementsxPerformance.0https://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh850988411 aTayabji, S. D.q(Shiraz D.),0https://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/n85005582eauthor.2 aERES Consultants, Inc.0https://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/n841084521 aUnited States.bFederal Highway Administration.bOffice of Infrastructure Research and Development,0https://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/no99081415esponsoring body.2 aTurner-Fairbank Highway Research Center,0https://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/n82270079eissuing body.08iPrint version:aAli, Hesham A.tDetermination of frost penetration in LTPP test sections. Final reportw(OCoLC)4238647308iMicrofiche version:aAli, Hesham A.tDetermination of frost penetration in LTPP test sectionsw(OCoLC)4348376240uhttps://purl.fdlp.gov/GPO/gpo924004 zAddress at time of PURL creationuhttps://www.fhwa.dot.gov/publications/research/infrastructure/pavements/ltpp/99088  3(online)uhttps://catalog.gpo.gov/fdlpdir/locate.jsp?ItemNumber=0982-G-11&SYS=001059562  aC0bGPO  aXZL4  abc76 20180601b20180601  aPERM_INGEST_0428202201843nam a2200445 i 00105957820180924105708.0m     o  d f      cr |||||||||||180924s2017    dcu     ob   f000 0 eng c  a(OCoLC)1054104524  aGPObengerdaepncGPO  apcc  an-us---  a0983-G-98 (online)0 aTD 2.30/5:17-011  aFHWA-PL-17-01100aFunding federal-aid highways. 1a[Washington, D.C.] :bU.S. Department of Transportation, Federal Highway Administration,c2017.  a1 online resource (iv, 76 pages)  atextbtxt2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr