tps://catalog.gpo.gov/fdlpdir/locate.jsp?ItemNumber=0982-G-11&SYS=001060415  aC0bGPO  aXZL4  abc76 20180608b2018060804255cam a2200589Ii 00106043020180718121040.0m     o  d f      cr |||||||||||180608e200007  vaua    obt  f000 0 eng d  a(OCoLC)1039097208  aGPObengerdaepncGPO  an-us---  a0982-G-11 (online)0 aTD 2.30:03-0940 aTD 2.30:00-0541 aHajek, Jaroslav J.,10aEstimating cumulative traffic loads, final report /cJerry J. Hajck [and three others]. 1aMcLean, VA :bU.S. Department of Transportation, Federal Highway Administration, Research, Development, and Technology, Turner-Fairbank Highway Research Center,cJuly 2000.  a1 online resource (2 volumes) :billustrations  atextbtxt2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier  aFinal report;bSept. 1998 to Aug. 1999.  aDescription based on online resource; title from PDF cover (FHWA.DOT.gov website, viewed June 08, 2018).  a"Performing organization: ERES Consultants, Inc."--Technical report documentation page.  a"Contracting Officer's Technical Representative (COTR): Cheryl Allen Richter"--Technical report documentation page.  a"July 2000"--Phase 1.  a"March 2005"--Phase 2.  a"Publication no. FHWA-RD-00-054"--Phase 1.  a"Publication no. FHWA-RD-03-094"--Phase 2.  a"The knowledge of traffic loads is a prerequisite for the pavement analysis process, especially for the development of load-related distress prediction models. This report describes a procedure for obtaining axle load spectra for Long Term Pavement Performance (LTPP) sections. The procedure has been demonstrated and evaluated by applying it to 12 LTPP sections for which different amounts of monitoring traffic data were available"--Technical report documentation page.  a"Phase 1 encompassed the development of the estimation methodology, including numerical examples, and was documented in report FHWA-RD-00-054 issued in July 2000. Phase 2, described in this report, included the assessment of the overall quality of traffic data for all 890 LTPP traffic sites, and the projection of axle loads for all LTPP sites with adequate traffic data"--Phase 2, technical report documentation page.  aIncludes tables.  aIncludes bibliographical references.00gphase 1.tEstimating cumulative traffic loads, final report --gphase 2.tVolume II: traffic data assessment and axle load projection for the sites with acceptable axle weight data, final report.  aSponsored by Office of Infrastructure Research and Development, Federal Highway AdministrationbDTFH61-96-C-00003 0aTraffic surveyszUnited States. 0aPavementsxLive loadszUnited StatesxTesting.2 aERES Consultants, Inc.0https://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/n841084521 aUnited States.bFederal Highway Administration.bOffice of Infrastructure Research and Development,0https://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/no99081415esponsoring body.2 aTurner-Fairbank Highway Research Center,0https://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/n82270079eissuing body.08iPrint version:aHajek, Jerry J.tEstimating cumulative traffic loadsw(OCoLC)4489145808iPrint version:tEstimating cumulative traffic loads. Volume II, Traffic data assessment and axle load projection for the sites with acceptable axle weight dataw(OCoLC)5913382240uhttps://purl.fdlp.gov/GPO/gpo925904 zAddress at time of PURL creation3Phase 1 (final report)uhttps://www.fhwa.dot.gov/publications/research/infrastructure/pavements/ltpp/00054/00054.pdf4 zAddress at time of PURL creation3Phase 2 (volume II)uhttps://www.fhwa.dot.gov/publications/research/infrastructure/pavements/ltpp/03094/03094.pdf  3(online)uhttps://catalog.gpo.gov/fdlpdir/locate.jsp?ItemNumber=0982-G-11&SYS=001060430  aC0bGPO  aGPOO  abc76 20180608b20180608  abc76 2018071803381cam a2200577Ki 00106043820191121112403.0m     o  d f      cr bn||||||abpcr bn||||||ada160515e199907  vaua    obft f000 0 eng d  a(OCoLC)949841091  aOCLCEbengerdaepncOCL